geoChess for Veranda
====================

geoChess is a chess game for GEOS 64/128 by Scott Hutter (November 2023,
https://github.com/geos64128/geochess), with contributions from the
authors in this repository's history. Its source comments say: "You are
free to modify this code as desired, as long as original author credit
is mentioned for both the GEOS code and the included AI engines." The
upstream repository has no licence file; no licence is stated there.

The chess engine (src/geochess-ai.h) is derived from BMCP v1.0 by Maksim
Korzh (https://www.chessprogramming.org/BMCP), itself based on ideas from
micro-Max by H.G. Muller; its header carries Maksim Korzh's notice (the
WTFPL, version 2).

This branch ("veranda") is the Veranda port of geoChess: Veranda is a
GEOS-style desktop for the Commander X16 (640x480). The port is
published and released with Veranda under the permission quoted above,
with credit to Scott Hutter for geoChess and to Maksim Korzh for the
BMCP engine it is derived from. The port's files
(veranda/, tools/, the changes to src/ marked "Veranda port") are kept
with geoChess and are NOT covered by Veranda's MIT licence; nothing of
geoChess is part of Veranda's repository. veranda/test/play.s is adapted
from Veranda's own test player (tests/sdk_play.s, MIT).

